  "question": {
    "math_academy_id": "q-8093",
    "knowledge_point_id": "7c9849b9-397b-5fb9-bb4b-01f3d013c5c2",
    "knowledge_point": "Computing the Image of a Polygon Under the Action of a Linear Transformation",
    "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990291/assets/369dde2e95b52356b71972b8f1103430e0a840d3d0478626dc5a78cba0f51a41.png)\n\nConsider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe quadrilateral $ABCD$ is shown above. Which of the following is ${A}^{′}{B}^{′}{C}^{′}{D}^{′},$ the image of $ABCD$ under the action of $T?$",
    "worked_solution": "To find the image of $T$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $ABCD:$\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 4 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 4 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 6 & 8 & 5\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${A}^{′}{B}^{′}{C}^{′}{D}^{′}$ are $(-1,3),(0,6),(0,8),(-1,5)$, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990291/assets/3caf43c4c62614f0c38b2f32c12892820ab4ae732669767b0d50104c85eee605.png)",
